  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If a replacement effect would try to replace a card that you can't draw, that effect can't apply.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you draw a card, and then Spirit of the Labyrinth enters the battlefield, you won't be able to draw more cards that turn.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you haven't drawn any cards in a turn, and a spell or ability would cause you to draw multiple cards, you'll just draw one card.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can draw a maximum of one card on each player's turn. Subsequent card draws are ignored.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you target yourself, this spell has no useful effect. It will not cause an infinite loop since a replacement effect can’t modify the same event more than once. This effect will not modify the draw that it has you perform.",
      "oracle_id": "ba4f9450-d468-4686-9f48-00fa08c6ac52",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you and your opponent each cast Plagiarize on each other during the same turn, the two spells effectively cancel each other out. You will draw cards when you normally would and so will your opponent.",
      "oracle_id": "ba4f9450-d468-4686-9f48-00fa08c6ac52",
      "published_at": "2007-07-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you target a player whose library is empty, any effect or turn-based action that would cause that player to draw a card will cause you to draw a card instead. It doesn’t matter that the other player would be unable to draw.",
      "oracle_id": "ba4f9450-d468-4686-9f48-00fa08c6ac52",
      "published_at": "2007-07-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You draw the card from your library as normal, not from your opponent’s library.",
      "oracle_id": "ba4f9450-d468-4686-9f48-00fa08c6ac52",
      "published_at": "2007-07-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an opponent is instructed to draw a card then discard a card, and Notion Thief causes you to draw a card instead, that opponent still discards a card. The same is true of any other actions that opponent is instructed to do.",
      "oracle_id": "f8dab16e-1d50-443e-9431-8b6f1cf61c9c",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more players each control a Notion Thief and a player would draw a card other than the first one in their draw step, that player chooses one of the applicable Notion Thief effects to apply. Then the player whose Notion Thief's effect was chosen repeats this process among the remaining Notion Thief effects, and so on, until there are no more possible such effects to apply. Each effect can be applied to the card draw only once this way.",
      "oracle_id": "f8dab16e-1d50-443e-9431-8b6f1cf61c9c",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The above procedure means that if each player in a two-player game controls a Notion Thief and one would draw a card, it really will be that player who draws a card.",
      "oracle_id": "f8dab16e-1d50-443e-9431-8b6f1cf61c9c",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
